---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const updated = "6 November 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy - Hermes"
  description="What Hermes processes, why, how long it keeps it, and the choices patients and clinic staff have."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent-strong">
      Legal
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-extrabold text-ink">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Who is responsible</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Hermes is care-loop software used by your clinic. The clinic that
          ordered your screening is the data controller for your health
          information; Hermes processes it on the clinic's instructions. For any
          request about your record, contact that clinic first.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">What we process</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li>Your name, phone number and clinic identifier.</li>
          <li>Laboratory results, the marker and units, and the plain-language summary shown in the app.</li>
          <li>Appointments, referrals, secure messages and case notes written by clinic staff.</li>
          <li>Push notification tokens, app opens and acknowledgments.</li>
          <li>Staff account details: name, work email, role and assigned clinic.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Why we process it</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          To deliver your screening result, notify you, let you book or message
          your care team, and let the clinic follow the case through to
          sign-off. We also keep an audit trail of case actions so the clinic can
          show who did what and when.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Consent and choices</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The patient app asks for consent before a login code is sent, covering
          SMS and push notifications. You can withdraw consent at any time by
          telling your clinic. Withdrawing notification consent stops reminders
          and result alerts; your clinic can still contact you by other means.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Who sees it</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Clinic staff see only the cases for their assigned clinic. Platform
          administrators can see all clinics for support and governance. The
          laboratory that produced the result and service providers that send
          SMS or push notifications process the minimum needed to deliver the
          message. We do not sell personal data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Case and audit records follow your clinic's retention policy. Login
          codes expire after 10 minutes, patient sessions after 30 days, and
          webhook replay receipts are deleted after 24 hours. Deleting the app
          removes the token stored on your device but not the clinic's record.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Security</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Traffic is encrypted in transit. Lab feeds are signed with
          HMAC-SHA256 and a timestamp, session tokens are stored hashed, and
          every patient request is checked against the signed-in patient. Staff
          access is role- and clinic-scoped, and every case transition is
          audited.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You can ask for a copy of your record, correction of inaccurate
          details, deletion where the clinic is not required to keep it, or a
          restriction on processing. Contact your clinic's data protection
          contact. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to your national
          data protection authority.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink">Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We will update this page when the way we process data changes and show
          the new date above. Material changes will also be communicated by your
          clinic.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
